      "reasoning": "I'm on defense during my opponent's combat phase. They're attacking with a 4/4 Forest and a 5/2 Flexible Waterbender. I have only one untapped creature: Jeong Jeong, the Deserter (2/3), and one untapped land.\n\
\n\
Blocking the 5/2 Flexible Waterbender with Jeong Jeong would result in Jeong Jeong dying, which I want to avoid — he's a key part of my Lesson-matters synergy and provides firebending mana. The Forest is a 4/4, so Jeong Jeong can't block it profitably either.\n\
\n\
Since any block would be unfavorable and I'm not under immediate lethal pressure (taking 9 damage this turn brings me to 4 life, but I can stabilize next turn), I choose not to block and preserve my threat.\n\
\n\
