        "pool_size": 0,
        "reasoning": "We need to pick a card from pack 1. We have no context about colors, but choose likely strong pick. Let's evaluate cards.\n\
\n\
List:\n\
\n\
1 Swamp land - usually not drafted unless need black mana; but basic lands are unlimited so probably not pick.\n\
\n\
2 Yuyan Archers {1}{R} common: Reach, discard to draw. Some value.\n\
\n\
3 Foggy Swamp Hunters {3}{B} common: lifelink and menace if drawn two cards this turn. Conditional.\n\
\n\
4 Sandbenders' Storm {3}{W} common: choose destroy 4+ creature or \"Earthbend 3\" (turn land into 0/0 creature with 3+1/+1 counters). Earthbending is a mechanic? Might be good but 3 mana.\n\
\n\
5 Earthbending Lesson {3}{G} common: Earthbend 4, similar to above but 4 counters.\n\
\n\
6 It'll Quench Ya! {1}{U} common: counter unless pays 2. Good cheap counter.\n\
\n\
7 Mongoose Lizard {4}{R}{R} common: Menace, deals 1 damage to any target on ETB, mountaincycling. Decent but expensive.\n\
\n\
8 Origin of Metalbending {1}{G} common: destroy artifact/enchant or +1/+1+indestructible. Good utility.\n\
\n\
9 Sokka's Haiku {3}{U}{U} uncommon: Counter spell, draw a card, mill three, untap land. Strong.\n\
\n\
10 Professor Zei, Anthropologist {U/R}{U/R} uncommon: T discarding draw, and sacrifice for graveyard recursion. Flexible.\n\
\n\
11 Ember Island Production {3}{U}{U} uncommon: token copy of own or opponent creature, with modifications. Good.\n\
\n\
12 Master Piandao {4}{W} uncommon: First strike, top 4 reveal ally/equipment/lesson, can put one in hand. Probably synergy with those cards.\n\
\n\
13 Aang, Swift Savior {1}{W}{U} rare: Flash, Flying, airbend 1 other target creature or spell, waterbend 8 to transform. Good early.\n\
\n\
14 Fated Firepower {X}{R}{R}{R} mythic: Flash, X fire counters, damage boost when you would deal damage. Potentially powerful but X unknown. Usually mythic is a good pick if you have red and like X.\n\
\n\
Given no deck plan, likely we want a strong uncommon or rare. Aang seems versatile; Sokka's Haiku is a strong counter with draw. Firepower mythic could be strong if you have red spells.\n\
\n\
Without known colors, many cards are color-coded: red, blue, green, black, white, multicolor. But typical picks: pick a rare if you want to shape deck. Aang is cheap 2 mana and has flash. Firepower is variable but can be high cost.\n\
\n\
Since we have no other cards, choose a card that is likely to be good in any deck: maybe a removal like Sandbenders' Storm? But it's common.\n\
\n\
I'd pick card 9 Sokka's Haiku is powerful and versatile (counter plus card draw) and gives untap land. Good for any colors? It's blue only, requires you to be playing blue.\n\
\n\
Or pick Aang (rare) which is cheap and versatile, fits many colors (white/blue) but may be less strong than Sokka.\n\
\n\
Probably the best early pick is the mythic: Fated Firepower can be cast with X = 0? Actually X can be any, but you need to spend index; can be big if you have mana. However it's expensive maybe not immediate.\n\
\n\
Given typical drafting, strongest early pick is an uncommon that gives immediate advantage: Sokka's Haiku is strong. So choose 9.\n\
\n\
Thus output \"9\".",
